  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 3rd level, a dealer may conjure playing cards as a swift action. These cards are charged with a chaotic energy that explodes on contact. Throwing a playing card is a ranged attack that deals force damage + additional damage equal to the dealer’s Charisma bonus. This extra damage is multiplied on a critical hit. Each time he conjures one, he must draw a card from a deck of playing cards and look at it. Place all used cards in a discard pile. When the deck is empty, he shuffles all the cards back into the deck. A conjured card only remains until the end of the dealer’s turn. A dealer with the Quick Draw feat may conjure his cards as a free action. A dealer has no limit on the number of cards he may conjure per day. See Table: Billiard Weapons for the statistics of a conjured card.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/dealer#toc35\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
